      "etymology": "Descends from Old Japanese adjective *fosi* (classical ほし), attested in the Kojiki and Man'yōshū in the sense of 'desirable, wanted'. Modern ほしい (欲しい) generalized the attributive *-ki > -i* ending, and the auxiliary request pattern 〜てほしい is attested by 1686.",
